class:: MIRaFileAnalyzer
summary:: High-speed whole-audio-file MIR feature extraction engine
categories:: Analysis>MIR, Libraries>MIR
related:: Classes/MIRaPlot, Classes/MIRaGUI, Guides/MIRa-file-visualization

description::
MIRaFileAnalyzer performs high-speed Non-Real-Time (NRT) batch feature extraction on entire audio files. It compiles an optimized headless analysis graph and runs it via link::Classes/Score::.recordNRT using MIRa's native C++ signal-processing UGens, extracting multi-tier musical descriptors at rates exceeding 50x real-time.

Extracted features include:
list::
## strong::RMS Envelope::: Root-mean-square amplitude tracking.
## strong::Pitch F0 & Voicing::: Fundamental frequency in Hz, continuous confidence, and voicing probability via link::Classes/PitchYIN::.
## strong::Harmonic Pitch Class Profile (HPCP)::: 12-bin harmonic chromagram via link::Classes/HPCP::.
## strong::Constant-Q Spectrogram (CQT)::: Multi-octave logarithmic time-frequency matrix via link::Classes/CQT::.
## strong::Spectral Centroid & Flatness::: Brightness and noisiness via link::Classes/SpecCentroid2:: and link::Classes/SpecFlatness2::.
## strong::Transient Onsets::: Onset trigger events and timestamps via link::Classes/Onsets2::.
::

classmethods::

method:: analyze
Asynchronously analyzes an audio file and passes the results to a completion callback.
argument:: audioPath
Path to the audio file.
argument:: hopHz
Hop rate in Hertz (frames per second, default: 100 Hz, corresponding to a 10 ms analysis hop).
argument:: numCQT
Number of CQT frequency bins (default: 72 bins = 6 octaves at 12 bins/octave).
argument:: fmin
Minimum frequency of CQT analysis in Hz (default: 65.4 Hz = C2).
argument:: action
A link::Classes/Function:: evaluated on completion with a link::Classes/Dictionary:: containing the extracted data:
list::
## code::\path::: Resolved file path.
## code::\duration::: File duration in seconds.
## code::\sampleRate::: Sample rate in Hz.
## code::\numChannels::: Channel count.
## code::\times::: link::Classes/FloatArray:: of frame timestamps in seconds.
## code::\rms::: link::Classes/FloatArray:: of RMS amplitude.
## code::\pitch::: link::Classes/FloatArray:: of F0 in Hz.
## code::\pitchMIDI::: link::Classes/FloatArray:: of MIDI pitch values.
## code::\voicing::: link::Classes/FloatArray:: of binary voicing indicators.
## code::\confidence::: link::Classes/FloatArray:: of pitch confidence (0..1).
## code::\centroid::: link::Classes/FloatArray:: of spectral centroid in Hz.
## code::\flatness::: link::Classes/FloatArray:: of spectral flatness (0..1).
## code::\onsets::: link::Classes/Array:: of detected onset times in seconds.
## code::\chroma::: 2D Array code::[numFrames][12]:: of HPCP chroma power.
## code::\cqt::: 2D Array code::[numFrames][numCQT]:: of CQT magnitude.
::

method:: extractWaveformPeaks
Reads an audio file directly and returns an array of min/max sample peak pairs for high-performance waveform rendering.
argument:: audioPath
Path to the audio file.
argument:: numPeaks
Target number of peak sample pairs (default: 1000).
returns:: An link::Classes/Array:: of code::[minSample, maxSample]:: pairs.

examples::
code::
(
// Extract whole-file MIR features and inspect summary statistics:
var soundPath = MIRaGUI.soundPath("melody.wav");
MIRaFileAnalyzer.analyze(soundPath, action: { |data|
    "Analysis completed for: %".format(data[\path]).postln;
    "Duration: % seconds (% frames at 100 Hz)".format(data[\duration].round(0.01), data[\times].size).postln;
    "Detected onsets: %".format(data[\onsets].size).postln;
    "Pitch range: % Hz to % Hz".format(
        data[\pitch].select({ |f| f > 0 }).minItem.round(0.1),
        data[\pitch].maxItem.round(0.1)
    ).postln;
});
)
::
